\title{From Analysis & Topology}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2023-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{If the partials #{u_x, u_y, v_x, v_y} exist and are continuous on #{U}, then #{u, v} are differentiable on #{U}. So it suffices to check that the partials are continuous and the Cauchy–Riemann equations hold to deduce complex differentiability.}
